cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference this QA study, please cite it as below. The original proofs belong to OpenAI; cite their repository for the mathematics."
type: dataset
title: "Scientific QA Evidence: independent reproduction of OpenAI's Navier–Stokes and Euler Lean proofs, with numerical mutation testing"
authors:
  - family-names: Guerra
    given-names: Cristian
    alias: criguex
    city: Medellín
    country: CO
repository-code: "https://github.com/criguex/scientific-qa-evidence"
url: "https://github.com/criguex/scientific-qa-evidence"
date-released: 2026-10-20
abstract: >-
  A software-QA reproduction package. It rebuilds OpenAI's Lean 4 formalizations
  of finite-time blowup for Navier–Stokes (Clay alternatives C and D) and Euler
  from a pinned commit, rechecks the configured challenges with Comparator using
  the Lean kernel and nanoda, includes a wrong-proof control fixture, and reports
  a paired macOS/Linux mutation-testing campaign over nine synthetic numerical
  models (84 variants per host: 27 PASS, 54 KILLED, 3 SURVIVED). It claims no new
  theorem and no scientific certification.
keywords:
  - software testing
  - quality assurance
  - reproducibility
  - mutation testing
  - formal verification
  - Lean 4
  - Navier–Stokes
references:
  - type: software
    title: "NavierStokesAndEuler: Lean certificates accompanying Navier–Stokes and Euler results"
    authors:
